      "Two releases in one week suggest on-device AI has crossed into real usefulness: a 2.6-billion-parameter model runs capable agents on a laptop in under 2.5 GB, and an 8 MB retriever indexes all of English Wikipedia in about seven minutes.",
    profile: "E3 T-Ac U2 H-Gr Z-Now",
    strength: "weak",
    logic: {
      what: "Liquid AI's LFM2.5-2.6B runs tool-using agents at 220 tokens per second on a laptop in under 2.5 GB, beating larger models on tool use.",
      mechanism:
        "A separate 8 MB static retriever indexed 6.4 million Wikipedia articles in 7 minutes on a MacBook Air, so capable local retrieval is now near-free.",
      soWhat:
        "For data residency, latency and per-call cost, more of the model can move on-device, onto hardware an enterprise already owns.",
    },
    sources: [
